## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/mirror.html
- Summary (EN): Mirrors an input image across a user-defined number of planes, creating symmetry such as radial patterns. By default it reflects the left side of the image across a vertical line down the middle.
- Résumé (FR) : Reproduit une image à travers un nombre donné de plans miroirs pour créer des symétries, comme des motifs radiaux, avec un angle cumulé et un décalage réglables.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the original layer to which the mirrors are applied"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: the layer type the source accepts", "Mode: Number and Offset (default) sets a total plane count with a shared angle and offset; Custom Mirror Planes configures each plane individually", "Number of Planes: total number of mirror planes in Number and Offset mode", "Mirrors: number of planes in Custom Mirror Planes mode, applied in list order", "Angle: in degrees; in Number and Offset mode each plane's angle accumulates (20 with 3 planes gives 20, 40 and 60). Positive values mirror the left side, negative values the right side", "Offset: perpendicular shift of the mirror plane from the origin in image space; positive shifts right, negative shifts left", "Reverse Mirror Plane Direction: flips the plane, so 180 behaves like 0"]

- Caveats: ["In Number and Offset mode angles are cumulative, so one value does not apply to every plane. The page gives the expression [-]180/ch(\"numberplanes\") to produce a full circle of radial symmetry.", "The page gives no explicit warnings or limitations."]

